Changelog: 14-11-2026 01:05:10

Fixed. The suite no longer names the suite for Windows devices (owner, 14-11-2026). The notes that said a feature
came from that suite's apps are gone from the six emulator managers, the portal, core and the tools; the examples in the
tools use this suite's own ps5- tags. Only comments and examples changed: no app works differently.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 00:49:37

Fixed. The suite no longer names the board it was ported from (owner, 14-11-2026: only CROSS-REFERENCE.md does). The
notes on where code came from are gone from core, HDMI CEC Manager, Fan Control, the tools and the tests; the
development stand-in's variable is PS5_REPLAY, and tools/ci_state.py asks GitHub as bazzite-console-ci-state. No app
works differently, except Bazzite Test (its CHANGELOG). Core loses wifi.py, the adapter reader only Bazzite Test
used. The older CHANGELOG entries of Bazzite Test, HDMI CEC Manager, Fan Control and System Overlay are reworded.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 00:36:00

Added. A release test cleans up after itself, and says what is installed. tools/check-release.sh on a machine without
the suite marks what it installs as a test's and removes it again when the portal closes: the apps installed during
the test, the portal and Bazzite Test, each with its own uninstaller. A machine that had the suite installed keeps
it, and --keep keeps a test's install. `check-release.sh status` lists what of the suite is installed and whether a
test put it there; `check-release.sh remove` removes the suite, with --purge its settings and logs too. Test:
tools/installer-tests/release-check.sh.

Fixed. Testing a portal release that is still a draft works. `check-release.sh release` stopped with "has no
ps5-portal-v0.2.2.tar.gz yet" (GitHub answers 404 for a draft's files): it now sees the draft and tests that, and
says to publish it after the test.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:59:57

Fixed. The wiki describes the suite as it is. The Install page is written for someone installing for the first time:
one block to paste into a terminal that downloads the newest published portal, checks it and installs it, then how
to install the apps, update and uninstall. Installing from a checkout moved to the Development chapter. The home page
presents the portal and all the apps by category instead of Bazzite Test alone. The Portal chapter no longer
describes the Media category and its launcher cards, which the portal does not have, and lists the header's symbols,
the settings and the controls in tables. The README has an Install section and no longer the Media trademarks. Two
dead links in the home page's footer are fixed.

Fixed. The Install page names the newest published portal release (the newest portal tag), not the version in
portal/VERSION, which is a draft until it is published: the link was dead in between. Publishing a portal release
builds the wiki again (docs.yml). tools/tests/test_wiki_apps.py keeps the wiki's and the README's app lists equal to
portal/apps.toml.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:40:46

Fixed. A test of Xbox Remote Play compared the app's version with the fixed number 0.1.0, so CI failed on the
commit that released 0.1.1 and the release run stopped before it built anything. The test compares the version in
the code with the VERSION file.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:28:59

Added. A release workflow of this repository's own, .github/workflows/release.yml, which Nexus Release Tool's Start
new release starts on the release commit. One run waits for CI on the commit, builds and publishes every app whose
pinned tag has no release yet, writes their checksums into portal/apps.toml in a commit "Pin ...", and builds the
portal from it as a draft, which the tool's Device test installs and its Publish makes the portal's release. A run
started again skips what is out already. Remote Play's native wheel is built in the run. tools/ci_state.py (whether
CI passed on a commit) and tools/release_commit.py (whether a commit only writes a release, so its parent's CI
counts) are this repository's own tools now, with their tests. The wiki's Development chapter has a Releases section.

Fixed. A portal release published by hand (tools/tag-release.sh) becomes GitHub's Latest release, where the app
releases' notes send people; every release was published as not the latest, so GitHub showed an app's on top.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:12:13

Fixed. The wiki's Install page links to the portal's own release and names its archive, from portal/VERSION when the
wiki is built ({{ portal_tag }} in a page, tools/mkdocs/hooks.py). It linked to the list of all releases, where an
app's release is on top.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 22:59:26

Fixed. tools/requirements-dev.txt names Pillow, which the test of tools/sync_icons.py needs: CI's tools job installs
only that file and failed on the import.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 22:54:30

Fixed. The wiki's chapters of Webcam, Controller and Remote Play show the app's icon above the title, as every other
app's chapter does.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 22:48:09

Fixed. The apps' icons and the portal's tile pictures are their categories' current pictures again: most were still
the earlier ones (the wiki's App categories page showed them). tools/sync_icons.py is back as this repository's own
tool and writes the copies from icons/<category>/ as icons/categories.toml assigns them; --check lists the ones that
differ, in CI and tools/ci-local.sh. categories.toml lists the suite's apps as portal/apps.toml does: Webcam and
Controller were missing, and three apps that are not in the suite were still listed. The wiki's icon (header, home
page and favicon) is the suite's current logo.

Added. .github/workflows/docs.yml builds the wiki from main and publishes it on GitHub Pages, at
robertotorino.github.io/bazzite-console/; until now nothing published it. The repository's Pages source must be
GitHub Actions. The wiki's Development chapter says so, and has a section on the icons.

Fixed. The portal tour's --wiki copy failed with "No such file or directory": docs/videos/ did not exist and
tools/portal_tour.py made only the poster's folder. It makes both.

Fixed. The root requirements-dev.txt installs what the development apps in dev/ need too (obsws-python and dbus-fast
for Nexus Demo Recorder, which said the OBS WebSocket client was missing).

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:55:19

Fixed. tools/ci-local.sh runs every test of the development apps: Nexus Release Tool's and Nexus Sound Lab's, which
it left out, and all of Nexus Deps's, of which it ran one file. Nexus Release Tool's and Nexus Deps's had gone stale
unnoticed since the suite got its own tooling back (58 and 31 tests failing); their CHANGELOGs say what was wrong.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:45:19

Fixed. tools/tag-release.sh builds Remote Play's release. It built the native wheel with --features decoder alone,
which replaces the features pyproject.toml names, so maturin made cffi bindings instead of the Python module and
stopped ("only supports one of the following syntax: #define PACKET_LOSS_MAX"). It now passes python,
pyo3/extension-module and decoder, with --locked and --compatibility linux. It also asked for maturin on the PATH,
where the development machine has it only in the virtual environment (apps/remoteplay/requirements-dev.txt): it takes
that one when the PATH has none.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:18:02

Fixed. Nexus Release Tool's Commit step works again: it runs tools/fix-modes.sh after git add, and the script did not
come back with the other tools when the suite got its own tooling again ("tools/fix-modes.sh: No such file or
directory"). It is back, and marks every .sh executable in the git index. Six scripts were not executable, in the
working tree or in git: tools/git-setup.sh (the tool's pull runs it first, and would have stopped there),
tools/ci-qt-libs.sh, tools/installer-tests/clb.sh and the install.sh of Fan Control, System Overlay and HDMI CEC
Manager, which a release's ./install.sh needs. They are now.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:05:30

Breaking. The suite stands on its own again, with its own tooling (owner, 13-11-2026: the repository is and stays
standalone; the entry below, the tools taken from a Nexus checkout, is undone). Back in the repository: the tools in
tools/ (apply_design.py, app_tour.py, build_release.py, check_versions.py, ci-local.sh, ci-qt-libs.sh, git-setup.sh,
stage_app.py, suites.py, tag-release.sh, tour_frames.py, the design panel and the disclaimer hook) with their tests,
the CHANGELOG merge driver and check, and the development apps in dev/. ci.yml checks out this repository alone
again, and tests Fan Control, System Overlay and HDMI CEC Manager with the other apps; release.yml and NEXUS_REF are
gone: a release is built and published with tools/tag-release.sh, as before. The wiki builds with the repository's
own hooks, and every address names this repository: github.com/RobertoTorino/bazzite-console for the releases, and
robertotorino.github.io/bazzite-console/ for the wiki. The installer tests stage with the repository's own
tools/stage_app.py. CLAUDE.md describes the standalone repository. What the entry below fixed stays: the addresses
that did not exist, the three apps' wiki chapters, installer tests and lines in the lists, the Media cards out of
the wiki and the README, Bazzite Test's installer test, the "Changes the board" comparison and Bazzite Test's pin.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 20:18:54

Breaking. The suite uses the Nexus tools from Nexus and keeps no copy of them (owner, 13-11-2026: one repository per
suite, the tooling in Nexus). It is worked on inside a Nexus checkout, cloned there as bazzite-console/, and every
job of its workflows starts with Nexus's action, which checks out Nexus at the commit NEXUS_REF names and this
repository inside it. Removed: the copies of the Nexus tools in tools/ (apply_design.py, app_tour.py,
build_release.py, check_versions.py, ci-local.sh, ci-qt-libs.sh, git-setup.sh, stage_app.py, suites.py,
tag-release.sh, tour_frames.py, the design panel and the disclaimer hook) with their tests, the CHANGELOG merge
driver and check (merge_changelog.py, check_changelogs.py: Nexus has none), the copies of the Nexus apps in dev/ with
their own core, and eight stray files at the root. The suite's own tools stay, and its core stays its own
(core/bazzite_console_core): the Nexus tools bundle it. ci.yml is written again for the Nexus checkout, with a job for
the Nexus tools' tests, and release.yml is new (a release commit started by hand, or a tag); a release is built by
GitHub, no longer by tag-release.sh on this machine. The wiki takes the Nexus tools' hooks and is published by
Nexus's docs.yml at robertotorino.github.io/nexus/bazzite-console-suite/. New at the root: CLAUDE.md and NEXUS_REF;
.gitattributes is Nexus's.

Fixed. Every address named github.com/RobertoTorino/nexus-console and robertotorino.github.io/nexus-console, which
do not exist: the repository is RobertoTorino/bazzite-console (the core's SUITE_REPO_URL, where the apps and the
portal look for releases; the READMEs' badges; the wiki). Fan Control, System Overlay and HDMI CEC Manager, listed in
portal/apps.toml, now have their wiki chapter, their installer test and their line in the README, the wiki's app list
and its categories. The wiki and the README no longer describe Media cards: the portal has none. The installer
tests stage with the Nexus tools; Bazzite Test's and the release test expect the app in /opt, where its installer
puts it. tools/check_manifest.py compares a "Changes the board" box with the manifest's text whatever its line
breaks. portal/apps.toml names Bazzite Test's next release, ps5-bazzite-v0.2.0, its VERSION (owner, 13-11-2026).
